# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ExamSphere — .dockerignore 
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This file tells the Docker build daemon which files to EXCLUDE from the
# "build context" that is sent to the daemon before building the image.
# 
# Why this matters:
#   • Smaller build context = faster `docker build` invocations.
#   • Prevents secrets (.env.local) from being accidentally baked into images.
#   • Prevents the host's compiled artifacts from polluting the clean
#     in-container build (especially important for cross-platform builds).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── Version Control ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The .git directory contains the full repository history. It is large, never
# needed during a Docker build, and can contain sensitive commit metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes


# ── Node Modules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules is always reinstalled inside the container (see `deps` stage).
# Including it would:
#   1. Massively inflate the build context size (often 200 MB+).
#   2. Potentially ship native addons compiled for the wrong OS.
#   3. Prevent the Docker layer cache from correctly invalidating when
#      dependencies change.
node_modules
.npm


# ── Next.js Build Artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .next/ contains the compiled output from a previous local build.
# It must NOT be copied into the builder stage because:
#   1. It might be stale or compiled for a different environment.
#   2. It can contain absolute host paths baked into chunk manifests.
#   3. It adds significant size to the build context.
# The builder stage runs `npm run build` to produce a fresh, clean build.
.next
out


# ── Environment & Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CRITICAL: Never ship local environment files into an image.
# .env.local can contain real API keys, database credentials, and tokens.
# These files are intentionally excluded to prevent secret leakage.
# Use Docker build args (ARG/ENV in Dockerfile) or runtime env vars instead.
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
.env.*.local

# The example file is safe to include (it contains no real secrets),
# but we exclude it too since it adds no value to the build.
.env.example
.env.local.example


# ── Development & Testing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test coverage reports and test runner artefacts are never needed in production.
coverage
.nyc_output
__tests__
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.spec.ts
*.spec.tsx
jest.config.*
vitest.config.*
playwright.config.*
cypress/
e2e/


# ── Documentation & Metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Documentation files add weight to the build context without serving any
# runtime purpose. Exclude them to keep builds lean.
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
LICENSE
*.md
docs/


# ── IDE & Editor Configuration ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editor configuration is purely for developer tooling on the host machine.
# Including these would pollute the image with irrelevant files.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.editorconfig


# ── OS-generated Files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS, Windows, and Linux all generate various metadata/cache files.
# These are meaningless inside a Linux container.
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Log files generated by npm, yarn, or the app during local development.
# They are noisy and irrelevant to the build.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
*.log
logs/


# ── Lint & Format Config (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# These are build-time dev tools. They ARE needed in the builder stage
# only if `npm run build` invokes ESLint (next.config.ts: ignoreDuringBuilds:false).
# If ESLint runs during build, comment these lines out.
# .eslintrc*
# eslint.config.*
# .prettierrc*
# .prettierignore


# ── TypeScript Build Info ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Incremental TypeScript compilation cache files — host-specific and useless
# inside the container.
*.tsbuildinfo


# ── Miscellaneous ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel deployment config — not relevant for Docker deployments.
.vercel

# Docker Compose files — not needed inside the image itself.
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*

# Yarn v2+ managed directories
.yarn/cache
.yarn/unplugged
.yarn/build-state.yml
.yarn/install-state.gz
.pnp.*

# Agent configuration files (Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, etc.)
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.agents/
